WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:08.200
Hanji is traditional Korean paper made from mulberry fibers. When it touches a Teflon film and separates, electricity is generated.

2
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:15.000
Unlike sensors that need external power, this one makes its own signal just from being pressed and released.

3
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:22.400
Comparing several kinds of hanji, thinner, more porous paper gave more power than thick, dense paper.

4
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:32.500
The best device delivered 13.2 microwatts per square centimeter, stayed stable over seventy two thousand presses, and lit 143 LEDs.

5
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:40.100
Machine learning on the sensor signals predicted foot health status with 95.94 percent accuracy.

6
00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:45.600
A traditional paper now makes its own electricity and reads our steps.
